DAT
id=qid::label=str::text=lstr::
25334::$$$message_0185_0000_0000$$$::The druid said...[lr]::
25335::$$$message_0185_0000_0001$$$::On this day, the young spear-bearer would gain all the glory and fortune he desired.[lr]::
25336::$$$message_0185_0000_0002$$$::Until the day the sea covers this land and this era, neither man, bird, nor flower will forget him.::
25337::$$$message_0185_0001_0000$$$::There will be no one who does not know his name in the five kingdoms...[lr]::
25338::$$$message_0185_0001_0001$$$::...no woman whom he doesn't love, and no man who fails to boast of him.[lr]::
25339::$$$message_0185_0001_0002$$$::The flash of his spear will be the pride of the Red Branch.[lr]::
25340::$$$message_0185_0001_0003$$$::The roar of his chariot will make the cattle raiders tremble.[lr]::
25341::$$$message_0185_0001_0004$$$::The beloved Child of Light.[lr]::
25342::$$$message_0185_0001_0005$$$::His hands will seize only glory.[lr]::
25343::$$$message_0185_0001_0006$$$::Never will he bend a knee, until the moment of his death.::
25344::$$$message_0185_0002_0000$$$::...But know this, babe of hazel[line len=2][lr]::
25345::$$$message_0185_0002_0001$$$::Your glory will burn out as quickly as the shimmering of the stars.[lr]::
25346::$$$message_0185_0002_0002$$$::In exchange for valor greater than any man, [l]you will pass into the horizon more swiftly than any man...::
25347::$$$message_0185_0003_0000$$$::                                           It was spring, six years ago.[lr]::
25348::$$$message_0185_0003_0001$$$::                                           I met a strange man.::
25349::$$$message_0185_0004_0000$$$::It had been two years since I was invited to the Mage's Association.[lr]::
25350::$$$message_0185_0004_0001$$$::I was granted a position only in name, and shunned without anything else asked of me.[lr]::
25351::$$$message_0185_0004_0002$$$::They treated me no differently from a curio with no practical use.[lr]::
25352::$$$message_0185_0004_0003$$$::I was handled like an antique with noble origins, but as a result, nobody wanted to actually use me, so I was stowed away in a warehouse and forgotten. ::
25353::$$$message_0185_0005_0000$$$::Of course, that didn't matter.[lr]::
25354::$$$message_0185_0005_0001$$$::I was afraid that I would rust away, so I left my hometown behind.[lr]::
25355::$$$message_0185_0005_0002$$$::Without knowing anything about the outside world, I had a vague sense of wanting to accomplish something, so I left.::
25356::$$$message_0185_0006_0000$$$::I had no value because I was a curio.[lr]::
25357::$$$message_0185_0006_0001$$$::To acquire value, I simply needed to demonstrate my utility.[lr]::
25358::$$$message_0185_0006_0002$$$::I took the initiative to show what I could do, taking on the role of a bloody cleaner despised by many mages.[lr]::
25359::$$$message_0185_0006_0003$$$::Practical use of magecraft in combat.[lr]::
25360::$$$message_0185_0006_0004$$$::Such was my specialty. I've always been more talented at it than other people.::
25361::$$$message_0185_0007_0000$$$::And so...[lr]::
25362::$$$message_0185_0007_0001$$$::...after several violent incidents, the Mage's Association recognized my value and gave me a job.[lr]::
25363::$$$message_0185_0007_0002$$$::The noble Lords governing the Association decreed it elegantly, condescendingly, as if to chase out a troublemaker.[lr]::
25364::$$$message_0185_0007_0003$$$::They made an exception and named Bazett Fraga McRemitz a Seal Designation Enforcer, despite my young age.::
25365::$$$message_0185_0008_0000$$$::Seal Designation.[lr]::
25366::$$$message_0185_0008_0001$$$::A title granted to mages with special talents, and an edict handed down by the Association.[lr]::
25367::$$$message_0185_0008_0002$$$::The Association issues these warrants to "preserve" those practitioners of magecraft which cannot be learned through study[line len=2]bearers of singular, once-in-a-generation abilities only possible thanks to the bearer's lineage or bodily traits.::
25368::$$$message_0185_0009_0000$$$::It sounds nice on paper, but in reality, it means incarceration.[lr]::
25369::$$$message_0185_0009_0001$$$::The Association treats Seal Designated mages as valuable research samples for posterity, ordering them to be captured and preserved with their abilities intact.[lr]::
25370::$$$message_0185_0009_0002$$$::To put it bluntly, it isn't much different from being pickled in a jar of formaldehyde.::
25371::$$$message_0185_0010_0000$$$::A Seal Designation is issued out of good intentions from the Association's point of view, but it's basically a death sentence for the chosen mage.[lr]::
25372::$$$message_0185_0010_0001$$$::The majority of such mages become fugitives to evade the Association's edict.[lr]::
25373::$$$message_0185_0010_0002$$$::Not because of the death sentence, however.[lr]::
25374::$$$message_0185_0010_0003$$$::Seal Designated individuals are all prominent mages.[lr]::
25375::$$$message_0185_0010_0004$$$::They prioritize their research of the arcane. They don't care about their own lives.[lr]::
25376::$$$message_0185_0010_0005$$$::They spend their lives obsessed with their research, so a Seal Designation is preposterous. Getting preserved in a jar of formaldehyde means that you can't continue to study magecraft.::
25377::$$$message_0185_0011_0000$$$::For this reason, they go on the run from the Association.[lr]::
25378::$$$message_0185_0011_0001$$$::Their goal is obvious: [lr]::
25379::$$$message_0185_0011_0002$$$::To disappear and hide somewhere they can pursue their research to their heart's content, and take it as far as it will go.::
25380::$$$message_0185_0012_0000$$$::The mages who receive Seal Designations and go on the run largely fall into two categories.::
25381::$$$message_0185_0013_0000$$$::The first type completely vanish, going into hiding to conceal their magecraft and only sharing it within their own bloodline.[lr]::
25382::$$$message_0185_0013_0001$$$::These are the fallen mages.[lr]::
25383::$$$message_0185_0013_0002$$$::We have to find and secure them before their abilities are lost, but on the other hand, they're virtually no threat.[lr]::
25384::$$$message_0185_0013_0003$$$::The Association only goes after them because of their considerable talents.::
25385::$$$message_0185_0014_0000$$$::The second type are sages who hole up in their own territory and pursue their magecraft to the maximum extent they can.[lr]::
25386::$$$message_0185_0014_0001$$$::These are exemplary mages who aim for ever greater heights.[lr]::
25387::$$$message_0185_0014_0002$$$::If allowed to continue honing their talents, they would probably accomplish great feats for the Association in no time at all.[lr]::
25388::$$$message_0185_0014_0003$$$::However, morals and justice don't exist to these people.[lr]::
25389::$$$message_0185_0014_0004$$$::The only thing that matters to these out-of-control sages is the realization of Mystics, even if they have to sacrifice uninvolved people to do it.::
25390::$$$message_0185_0015_0000$$$::...Now that is problematic.[lr]::
25391::$$$message_0185_0015_0001$$$::Still, with regard to those that behave and perform well, the Association could decide to just keep an eye on them. They'll be left alone until they generate results. The Association's primary goal still is arcane research, after all.::
25392::$$$message_0185_0016_0000$$$::But if it doesn't go well[line len=2]if the prime directive of the Mage's Association to conceal Mystics is violated, then the Association will move swiftly to put a stop to their folly.[lr]::
25393::$$$message_0185_0016_0001$$$::It isn't only to stop the knowledge of the occult from spreading.[lr]::
25394::$$$message_0185_0016_0002$$$::The Association needs to preserve their valuable property, even if it only means keeping their body.::
25395::$$$message_0185_0017_0000$$$::If the affair were publicly known, forces would appear to execute the sage in the name of justice.[lr]::
25396::$$$message_0185_0017_0001$$$::The greatest threat is the Holy Church's heretic hunters.[lr]::
25397::$$$message_0185_0017_0002$$$::They would incinerate not just the sage, but all of their knowledge.::
25398::$$$message_0185_0018_0000$$$::While it would achieve the same result of putting a stop to the sage's depravity, the ultimate goal is completely opposite to ours.[lr]::
25399::$$$message_0185_0018_0001$$$::While the Mage's Association and the Holy Church maintain a public nonaggression pact, they still have conflicts off the record.[lr]::
25400::$$$message_0185_0018_0002$$$::No, they're de facto still at war, assuming that it won't be recorded.::
25401::$$$message_0185_0019_0000$$$::As a result, my job involved both breaching the mad sages' dens, and fighting the Church's Executors.[lr]::
25402::$$$message_0185_0019_0001$$$::About a year into this occupation...[lr]::
25403::$$$message_0185_0019_0002$$$::I met a certain man from the enemy side during one of my Seal Designation enforcement missions.[lr]::
25404::$$$message_0185_0019_0003$$$::He was an Executor of the Holy Church,[lr]::
25405::$$$message_0185_0019_0004$$$::a priest whose job was to condemn all offenders in his god's name.::
25406::$$$message_0185_0020_0000$$$::"Why don't we work together, Miss?[lr]::
25407::$$$message_0185_0020_0001$$$::Each of us are the last survivors of our sides. It wouldn't be smart to crush each other now."[lr]::
25408::$$$message_0185_0020_0002$$$::The priest casually offered to cooperate with me.[lr]::
25409::$$$message_0185_0020_0003$$$::He'd lost all of his companions, while my team was nearly wiped out.[lr]::
25410::$$$message_0185_0020_0004$$$::We were the last survivors in the garden of a mage who had been using dead bodies to attempt to recreate souls.::
25411::$$$message_0185_0021_0000$$$::Normally, it would be unthinkable for an Executor to cooperate with the Mage's Association, no matter how dire the circumstances, without the authorization of a bishop or greater.[lr]::
25412::$$$message_0185_0021_0001$$$::Executors are the most pious of believers. In order to keep to their faith, they would never associate with a heretic like me.[lr]::
25413::$$$message_0185_0021_0002$$$::But this priest was different.[lr]::
25414::$$$message_0185_0021_0003$$$::Perhaps he had some familiarity with mages, because he didn't treat me with scorn. In fact, he smiled at me warmly like a comrade.::
25415::$$$message_0185_0022_0000$$$::"...I have no objections to working together.[lr]::
25416::$$$message_0185_0022_0001$$$::But we aren't allies. We'll end up fighting over the prize in the end. I can't trust someone like that to watch my back."[lr]::
25417::$$$message_0185_0022_0002$$$::My orders were to retrieve the Seal Designated mage.[lr]::
25418::$$$message_0185_0022_0003$$$::The priest was here to take his life.[lr]::
25419::$$$message_0185_0022_0004$$$::Even if we cooperated to reach the end, he would become my enemy.::
25420::$$$message_0185_0023_0000$$$::"There's no need for concern. My job is only to kill that man. I will leave the rest to you. What you do with the body is none of my concern."[lr]::
25421::$$$message_0185_0023_0001$$$::The priest said so candidly.[lr]::
25422::$$$message_0185_0023_0002$$$::He would just hand the body over to me.[lr]::
25423::$$$message_0185_0023_0003$$$::He would be satisfied as long as he was allowed to get rid of the mage's life, his soul.::
25424::$$$message_0185_0024_0000$$$::"...All right. I'll trust what you said."[lr]::
25425::$$$message_0185_0024_0001$$$::Did I understand the weight of those words?[lr]::
25426::$$$message_0185_0024_0002$$$::I surprised myself with how easily I agreed to his proposal.[lr]::
25427::$$$message_0185_0024_0003$$$::This man was dangerous. I could sense his venom, that he was nothing like a saint, but I still took the hand he offered.::
25428::$$$message_0185_0025_0000$$$::Later, I would come to think...[lr]::
25429::$$$message_0185_0025_0001$$$::...that he was indeed no saint.[lr]::
25430::$$$message_0185_0025_0002$$$::But, he was the only person I had ever met with strength that I respected.::
25431::$$$message_0185_0026_0000$$$::"I'm Bazett, a mage sent by the Association. You are...?"[lr]::
25432::$$$message_0185_0026_0001$$$::We introduced ourselves and made a temporary alliance.[lr]::
25433::$$$message_0185_0026_0002$$$::Two days later...[lr]::
25434::$$$message_0185_0026_0003$$$::We disposed of the mage playing with dead bodies and returned to our respective factions.::
25435::$$$message_0185_0027_0000$$$::To be honest, I had a feeling we would meet again.[lr]::
25436::$$$message_0185_0027_0001$$$::My job was to pursue Seal Designated mages.[lr]::
25437::$$$message_0185_0027_0002$$$::His job was to hunt heretics.[lr]::
25438::$$$message_0185_0027_0003$$$::He had knowledge of magecraft, so he was probably being deployed to hunt mages rather than Dead Apostles or the possessed.[lr]::
25439::$$$message_0185_0027_0004$$$::We were competing in the same field.[lr]::
25440::$$$message_0185_0027_0005$$$::One meeting was a coincidence.[lr]::
25441::$$$message_0185_0027_0006$$$::But two or three meetings must surely be an inevitability I hoped for.::
25442::$$$message_0185_0028_0000$$$::We only ever met when we were both alone.[lr]::
25443::$$$message_0185_0028_0001$$$::Of course, I was operating alone by this time, so he was the only one with allies that always perished before we met up.[lr]::
25444::$$$message_0185_0028_0002$$$::We fought side by side three times.[lr]::
25445::$$$message_0185_0028_0003$$$::We kept it a secret, never reporting it to our organizations.[lr]::
25446::$$$message_0185_0028_0004$$$::I trusted my judgment and allied with him.[lr]::
25447::$$$message_0185_0028_0005$$$::That trifling secret made me a little happy.::
25448::$$$message_0185_0029_0000$$$::"...And then, the boy had his coming-of-age ritual.[lr]::
25449::$$$message_0185_0029_0001$$$::A druid told the futures of those who became warriors that day.[lr]::
25450::$$$message_0185_0029_0002$$$::Their futures reflected in the river rapids were grim. He said that anyone who became a warrior that day would die early in exchange for achieving peerless glory."::
25451::$$$message_0185_0030_0000$$$::"All of the boys there were too scared to move, but one boy wasn't impressed by the prophecy. Without hesitation, he approached the king and demanded to be recognized as a warrior."::
25452::$$$message_0185_0031_0000$$$::"The king tried to stop the boy, but he wouldn't listen, and was named a warrior.[lr]::
25453::$$$message_0185_0031_0001$$$::The rest goes according to the myths. You know the heroic epic of the Hound of Ulster, don't you?"::
25454::$$$message_0185_0032_0000$$$::It was the night of the third time we fought together.[lr]::
25455::$$$message_0185_0032_0001$$$::The silence gnawed at me, so I talked about something unrelated to work.[lr]::
25456::$$$message_0185_0032_0002$$$::Somehow, I ended up talking about a folktale from my homeland.::
25457::$$$message_0185_0033_0000$$$::"No, I'm not too familiar with that. I've only heard the name before. I don't mind it as a bit of pillow talk, but I think your point lies elsewhere.[lr]::
25458::$$$message_0185_0033_0001$$$::...Yes, you probably felt frustrated by the boy's actions.[lr]::
25459::$$$message_0185_0033_0002$$$::Even now, in your adulthood, you're still afraid of his decision, aren't you?"::
25460::$$$message_0185_0034_0000$$$::The priest looked at me with a melancholy smile.[lr]::
25461::$$$message_0185_0034_0001$$$::"..."[lr]::
25462::$$$message_0185_0034_0002$$$::...I couldn't hide anything from this man. He could see right through me.[lr]::
25463::$$$message_0185_0034_0003$$$::I would normally find that fearsome, but having him know how I felt was comforting.::
25464::$$$message_0185_0035_0000$$$::"...I'm not afraid of it, exactly, but I don't understand what he was so fixated on.[lr]::
25465::$$$message_0185_0035_0001$$$::The prophecy said that he would achieve the highest glory, but also that he'd die earlier than anyone.[lr]::
25466::$$$message_0185_0035_0002$$$::But the boy didn't show any fear or hesitation, and told the king he wanted to become a warrior immediately."::
25467::$$$message_0185_0036_0000$$$::"When the king asked him why, he refused to answer, just insisting that he wanted to be a warrior.[lr]::
25468::$$$message_0185_0036_0001$$$::The coming-of-age ritual went on, but the boy didn't feel any hope or worry about the prophecy.[lr]::
25469::$$$message_0185_0036_0002$$$::It's like he didn't care about the prophecy at all. He was just happy to become a warrior, and at some point his reason for being a warrior disappeared.[lr]::
25470::$$$message_0185_0036_0003$$$::...Honestly, I don't know what he was looking at."::
25471::$$$message_0185_0037_0000$$$::Was he afraid of living a short life, but thought the glory would be worth it?[lr]::
25472::$$$message_0185_0037_0001$$$::Was he captivated only by the glory, and didn't care about how long he'd live?[lr]::
25473::$$$message_0185_0037_0002$$$::Or...::
25474::$$$message_0185_0038_0000$$$::"You want to know which was more important to him, glory or a short life?[lr]::
25475::$$$message_0185_0038_0001$$$::...Based on what you've told me, I think it's neither."[lr]::
25476::$$$message_0185_0038_0002$$$::"Neither...? Even though he made up his mind to become a warrior despite the prophecy?"::
25477::$$$message_0185_0039_0000$$$::"He didn't make up his mind. You said that he heard the prophecy and ran to the king without thinking about its contents, remember?[lr]::
25478::$$$message_0185_0039_0001$$$::That would imply the boy knew about the prophecy all along.[lr]::
25479::$$$message_0185_0039_0002$$$::He knew that's how his life would unfold. Don't you think he followed the druid's prophecy because he was certain of it from the day he was born?"::
25480::$$$message_0185_0040_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
25481::$$$message_0185_0040_0001$$$::He was certain from the day he was born.[lr]::
25482::$$$message_0185_0040_0002$$$::The boy didn't fear the druid's prophecy. He accepted the duty he was given without question.[lr]::
25483::$$$message_0185_0040_0003$$$::   That's right.[lr]::
25484::$$$message_0185_0040_0004$$$::What I was afraid of was the part of it that made me sad.[lr]::
25485::$$$message_0185_0040_0005$$$::It wasn't gallantry for choosing glory despite a short life that I found tragic.[lr]::
25486::$$$message_0185_0040_0006$$$::I pitied the hero who didn't even try to change his untimely destiny.::
25487::$$$message_0185_0041_0000$$$::"...I'm amazed. I've read that story countless times, but I never thought of that.[lr]::
25488::$$$message_0185_0041_0001$$$::...Maybe you resemble the boy in the story, somehow."[lr]::
25489::$$$message_0185_0041_0002$$$::"How rude. I'm not nearly that thoughtless."[lr]::
25490::$$$message_0185_0041_0003$$$::"Eh?"::
25491::$$$message_0185_0042_0000$$$::I couldn't believe my eyes.[lr]::
25492::$$$message_0185_0042_0001$$$::The priest muttered it sulkily, like I offended him.[lr]::
25493::$$$message_0185_0042_0002$$$::I think it was the first time I'd ever seen him show human emotion.::
25494::$$$message_0185_0043_0000$$$::"What? Do you disagree?"[lr]::
25495::$$$message_0185_0043_0001$$$::"Huh? No, my mistake. I was talking about your way of life. You seem to have a certain conviction about your life, like the boy."[lr]::
25496::$$$message_0185_0043_0002$$$::"...Oh? In what way?"[lr]::
25497::$$$message_0185_0043_0003$$$::"The way you don't need anyone else.[lr]::
25498::$$$message_0185_0043_0004$$$::You're determined to survive on your own until the very end.[lr]::
25499::$$$message_0185_0043_0005$$$::...You don't actually need my help. You're just with me because it's more efficient."::
25500::$$$message_0185_0044_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
25501::$$$message_0185_0044_0001$$$::The priest smiled gloomily again.[lr]::
25502::$$$message_0185_0044_0002$$$::His agreement was a little painful for me, even though I already knew it was true.::
25503::$$$message_0185_0045_0000$$$::...This was our third alliance. It didn't even last ten days, but I gained a painful awareness of what sort of person he was.[lr]::
25504::$$$message_0185_0045_0001$$$::This man never associated with other people.[lr]::
25505::$$$message_0185_0045_0002$$$::He didn't need anyone else, and he didn't hate anyone.[lr]::
25506::$$$message_0185_0045_0003$$$::He was an aberration who deviated from normal morals and feelings, with strength that made him a complete, independent person.[lr]::
25507::$$$message_0185_0045_0004$$$::But that's what made me so sure that he was, in one unmistakable word, [font italic=true]evil[font italic=false].::
25508::$$$message_0185_0046_0000$$$::...Even now, I'm not sure what attracted me to that dangerous man.[lr]::
25509::$$$message_0185_0046_0001$$$::But I couldn't help but think...[lr]::
25510::$$$message_0185_0046_0002$$$::That if this man who didn't need anyone needed me, it would be more comforting than anything else I could think of.::
25511::$$$message_0185_0047_0000$$$::"Is something on your mind?[lr]::
25512::$$$message_0185_0047_0001$$$::...I must say, you overly dwell on things. If you're finished talking, then go to sleep. You can take next watch in ninety minutes."::
25513::$$$message_0185_0048_0000$$$::The priest added fuel to the campfire.[lr]::
25514::$$$message_0185_0048_0001$$$::And then...[lr]::
25515::$$$message_0185_0048_0002$$$::"...Unfortunately, I'm a normal person. I can't live with confidence like yours. All I have are silly doubts.[lr]::
25516::$$$message_0185_0048_0003$$$::...Sometimes, even living feels like suffering."[lr]::
25517::$$$message_0185_0048_0004$$$::...I inadvertently voiced a deep, old insecurity.::
25518::$$$message_0185_0049_0000$$$::"..."[lr]::
25519::$$$message_0185_0049_0001$$$::He added fuel to the fire again.[lr]::
25520::$$$message_0185_0049_0002$$$::...That was a serious slip of the tongue. I'm sure I disappointed him. He reached out to me because I carry out my missions with cold efficiency.[lr]::
25521::$$$message_0185_0049_0003$$$::He didn't need someone who whined like this.::
25522::$$$message_0185_0050_0000$$$::...The silence was oppressive.[lr]::
25523::$$$message_0185_0050_0001$$$::I was too afraid to look at him.[lr]::
25524::$$$message_0185_0050_0002$$$::And then, as if I hadn't said anything significant...[lr]::
25525::$$$message_0185_0050_0003$$$::"Living is not suffering.[lr]::
25526::$$$message_0185_0050_0004$$$::You're too strict with yourself,"[lr]::
25527::$$$message_0185_0050_0005$$$::he declared with an emotionless yet earnest voice.::
25528::$$$message_0185_0051_0000$$$::"Huh...?"[lr]::
25529::$$$message_0185_0051_0001$$$::"Such strictness is not easily discarded. If you don't understand, then the only way is to learn of the world and measure it.[lr]::
25530::$$$message_0185_0051_0002$$$::Bazett Fraga McRemitz. If you think that this world does not need you, then you must travel to many worlds so that you can forgive yourself."::
25531::$$$message_0185_0052_0000$$$::Across the sea. Beyond the sky.[lr]::
25532::$$$message_0185_0052_0001$$$::He told me to leave my insignificant self and my insignificant country behind, to pack up and travel the world.[lr]::
25533::$$$message_0185_0052_0002$$$::Just like those ships that set on in search of undiscovered paradises beyond the sea.[lr]::
25534::$$$message_0185_0052_0003$$$::Those during the Age of Exploration.::
25535::$$$message_0185_0053_0000$$$::"Have you done it?"[lr]::
25536::$$$message_0185_0053_0001$$$::I find myself asking him.[lr]::
25537::$$$message_0185_0053_0002$$$::To continue the comparison, it's because I felt a conviction...[lr]::
25538::$$$message_0185_0053_0003$$$::A conviction that he had been through difficult times, like me.::
25539::$$$message_0185_0054_0000$$$::"No, I stopped trying... I was more desperate to find a way to atone in my youth, but ever since a major incident several years ago, I no longer needed to forgive myself."[lr]::
25540::$$$message_0185_0054_0001$$$::A major incident...?[lr]::
25541::$$$message_0185_0054_0002$$$::He didn't seem to be talking about hunting mages.[lr]::
25542::$$$message_0185_0054_0003$$$::This priest seemed to have fought in a great war that I don't know about.::
25543::$$$message_0185_0055_0000$$$::"...So, what about yourself were you trying to forgive?"[lr]::
25544::$$$message_0185_0055_0001$$$::"A bad habit I was born with. I'm incapable of loving anything, you see. I lack the morality that other people have. At the time, I couldn't tolerate that flaw."[lr]::
25545::$$$message_0185_0055_0002$$$::Not everything he said was in the past tense.[lr]::
25546::$$$message_0185_0055_0003$$$::He still couldn't love people.::
25547::$$$message_0185_0056_0000$$$::"...And you accepted that you couldn't fix that flaw?"[lr]::
25548::$$$message_0185_0056_0001$$$::"Yes. I may not be able to feel the love that other people do, but I can still find beauty in things. My standards are different from the rest of you, but I can still experience a form of love.[lr]::
25549::$$$message_0185_0056_0002$$$::It was idiotic of me to let it bother me, but I didn't realize it when I was younger."[lr]::
25550::$$$message_0185_0056_0003$$$::There was no doubt in his voice.[lr]::
25551::$$$message_0185_0056_0004$$$::He lamented his past, but had since moved on.::
25552::$$$message_0185_0057_0000$$$::"And you don't feel any doubt anymore?"[lr]::
25553::$$$message_0185_0057_0001$$$::"I no longer seek to forgive myself, but I want to know the reason one such as I am permitted to exist.[lr]::
25554::$$$message_0185_0057_0002$$$::If my life is my own... [l][say storage=snplg11_kot_0162 name=è¨€å³°]I wish to use the time I have left to find that answer."[lr]::
25555::$$$message_0185_0057_0003$$$::"But there's no one who can answer your questions, is there?"[lr]::
25556::$$$message_0185_0057_0004$$$::"I would say the one who can answer has yet to be born, but I hope that opportunity will come."::
25557::$$$message_0185_0058_0000$$$::His expression was warm.[lr]::
25558::$$$message_0185_0058_0001$$$::He stared at the flame as if caressing a baby.::
25559::$$$message_0185_0059_0000$$$::"...I didn't expect to hear you say that. I feel a little better knowing that even you don't have everything figured out."[lr]::
25560::$$$message_0185_0059_0001$$$::I smiled, feeling cheered up by his gentle expression.[lr]::
25561::$$$message_0185_0059_0002$$$::"I'm glad to hear that. I hope you found my more extensive life experience instructive."[lr]::
25562::$$$message_0185_0059_0003$$$::The priest closed his eyes in satisfaction.[lr]::
25563::$$$message_0185_0059_0004$$$::...Our unnecessary conversation ended there.[lr]::
25564::$$$message_0185_0059_0005$$$::It was time to return to our duties and prepare for tomorrow's battle.::
25565::$$$message_0185_0060_0000$$$::"I'll sleep first, then. Please wake me when it's time to rotate the watch."[lr]::
25566::$$$message_0185_0060_0001$$$::"I know. We're in enemy territory, so try not to dream too soundly."::
25567::$$$message_0185_0061_0000$$$::...I closed my eyes.[lr]::
25568::$$$message_0185_0061_0001$$$::My slumber was deeper than I expected. I must have been tired.[lr]::
25569::$$$message_0185_0061_0002$$$::I dreamed of my hometown.[lr]::
25570::$$$message_0185_0061_0003$$$::In my dream, I boarded a ship and left that gray, dilapidated port for another country.::
25571::$$$message_0185_0062_0000$$$::That was the last conversation I ever had with the priest.[lr]::
25572::$$$message_0185_0062_0001$$$::Our work plans never aligned again.[lr]::
25573::$$$message_0185_0062_0002$$$::...But I was sure another chance would come.[lr]::
25574::$$$message_0185_0062_0003$$$::We meshed well as business rivals.[lr]::
25575::$$$message_0185_0062_0004$$$::As long as he didn't die, and as long as I continued my Seal Designation work...[lr]::
25576::$$$message_0185_0062_0005$$$::I was sure that we would pick up that conversation again someday...:ŠkŒ